course: dictionary
lesson: 7914
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word rave is a good example. «She raved about the film» means she talked with great excitement and praise. It does not mean she was shouting mad.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In «He was raving about aliens», the word raving comes with a wild, muddled feeling, so it means talking wildly, as if he was not thinking clearly. Ask yourself which meaning fits the words around it.
explain: Rave can also be a noun, meaning a big loud party, or an adjective, as in «The show got rave reviews», where rave means full of praise. Try each meaning in the sentence. The one that makes sense is the right one.
fact: Rave (verb) means to talk with great excitement and praise about something you like.
fact: Rave (verb) can also mean to talk wildly or angrily, as if not thinking clearly.
fact: Rave (noun) means a big party with loud electronic dance music, often all night, mainly for adults.
fact: Rave (adjective) means full of praise, as in «rave reviews».
fact: «Raving mad» means completely crazy, as in «The March Hare won't be raving mad».
exercise: «She raved about the film for an hour.» What does raved mean here? | To fall asleep in the seats | *To talk with great excitement and praise | To feel cold and wet | To shout angrily at the cinema staff
exercise: Ella says, «The show got rave reviews.» What does rave mean in this sentence? | Very quiet | A big loud party | *Full of praise | Talking wildly
exercise: «Alice thinks the March Hare won't be raving mad.» What does raving mad mean? | Lost in a field | Very tired and sleepy | Happy and calm | *Completely crazy
test: «He was raving about aliens, and nobody could follow him.» What does raving mean here? | Walking very fast | Talking with great praise about something he liked | Painting a picture of aliens | *Talking wildly, as if not thinking clearly
test: Jayden went to a rave on Saturday night. What is a rave here? | A quiet picnic in the park | A long review of a book | A type of bird | *A big party with loud dance music, often all night
exam: «Maya could not stop raving about her new bike.» What does raving about mean here? | *Talking with great excitement and praise | Hiding it under her bed | Shouting in anger at the bike shop | Riding it through the rain
